          <declname>CreatePass</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Parses <computeroutput>Pipeline</computeroutput> as a comma-separated sequence of pass names and sets the pass pipeline, using <computeroutput>CreatePass</computeroutput> to instantiate passes by name. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Passes can have arguments, for example: &quot;pass1&lt;arg1,arg2&gt;,pass2,pass3&lt;arg3,arg4&gt;&quot;</para>
<para>The arguments between angle brackets are treated as a mostly opaque string and each pass is responsible for parsing its arguments. The exception to this are nested angle brackets, which must match pair-wise to allow arguments to contain nested pipelines, like:</para>
<para>&quot;pass1&lt;subpass1,subpass2&lt;arg1,arg2&gt;,subpass3&gt;&quot;</para>
<para>An empty args string is treated the same as no args, so &quot;pass&quot; and &quot;pass&lt;&gt;&quot; are equivalent. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
